Portions of this suite adapt patterns and, in a small number of clearly-noted
cases, verbatim phrasing from third-party sources studied during synthesis
(see README.md "Lineage" table for what was taken from each). Those projects
carry their own licenses; nothing here asserts ownership over their original
text. Grouped below by license class, kept compact:

MIT: ponytail, taste-skill, designer-skills, awesome-design-md,
kepano/obsidian-skills, tpitsunov/obsidian-skills, adriangrant/Obsidian-SKILLS,
ayghri/i-have-adhd, plannotator/effective-html, caveman (JuliusBrussee/caveman,
installed plugin), React Native docs, Expo docs, pmndrs/zustand,
obra/superpowers, wshobson/agents, davila7/claude-code-templates,
ibelick/ui-skills, mattpocock/skills, addyosmani/agent-skills,
redis/agent-skills (Redis Inc.), phuryn/pm-skills, emilkowalski/skills,
robzilla1738/supergoal, riverpod.dev (underlying repo rrousselGit/riverpod —
no CC BY grant found for the docs site itself, so the repo license governs).

Apache-2.0: pbakaus/impeccable; Android Developers docs (Google: the
documentation content specifically is Apache-2.0 — developer.android.com/
license — distinct from the CC BY 2.5 that covers only non-doc site content);
Anthropic html-effectiveness sample gallery; alibaba/open-code-review;
openai/skills; qdrant/skills; s3onghyun/otelcol-doctor; zuoyebang/aiweave;
yetone/kill-ai-slop; nexu-io/open-design.

Mixed, not MIT (Apache-2.0-licensed skills plus source-available components;
mechanisms re-expressed here, no files copied): anthropics/skills.

CC BY 4.0 (documentation, re-expressed not reproduced verbatim): Flutter docs
(docs.flutter.dev — the docs are what was actually harvested; the
flutter/flutter code repo is BSD-3 but was not the source used), dart.dev
linter-rules docs, agentskills/agentskills spec/schema doc.

CC BY-SA 4.0 (mechanisms re-expressed, no text copied — ShareAlike scope
limited to the re-expressed passages, not this suite as a whole):
trailofbits/skills.

CC BY-NC 4.0 (patterns re-expressed, no verbatim; NC restriction disclosed):
HackTricks.

CC0-1.0: PatrickJS/awesome-cursorrules, Solido/awesome-flutter.

Own material, not third-party: humanizer sources, the author's own prior PM skill.

impulse-devops cites public security advisories. Where a rule in this suite is a
close paraphrase or short verbatim line from one of the above, treat it as
inspired-by, not copied wholesale — the surrounding structure, the
ladder/baseline/register mechanisms, and the Go/Python/Vue-specific content
are original to this suite.
